WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.933
After defeating Valerie at the Laverre City Gym

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.466
with the help of Fletchinder and Hawlucha, Ash earned the Fairy Badge.

3
00:00:11.533 --> 00:00:16.500
Now our hero only needs two more Kalos Gym Badges to enter the Kalos League!

4
00:00:16.566 --> 00:00:18.800
And after observing Ash's hard-fought battle

5
00:00:18.866 --> 00:00:22.200
with all his creative strategies in full view,

6
00:00:22.266 --> 00:00:24.933
Sawyer seems to be highly motivated!

7
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.800
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

8
00:00:26.866 --> 00:00:28.566
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

9
00:00:28.633 --> 00:00:32.000
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

10
00:00:32.066 --> 00:00:33.466
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

11
00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:37.300
♪ There's only one way to tell this story ♪

12
00:00:37.366 --> 00:00:40.566
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

13
00:00:40.633 --> 00:00:44.000
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

14
00:00:44.066 --> 00:00:47.966
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

15
00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:52.666
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

16
00:00:52.733 --> 00:00:54.933
♪ Pokémon! ♪

17
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.966
Rivals, Today And Tomorrow!

18
00:01:11.466 --> 00:01:14.066
So that's what it takes to win a battle.

19
00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:16.000
Being able to think on your feet!

20
00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:22.233
All right! And then, one of these days, I'll...

21
00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.633
Aaargh!

22
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:24.966
-Pika?

23
00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:30.033
- Are you OK?
- Unh. Yeah. Yeah, I'm fine.

24
00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.166
I guess I wasn't looking.

25
00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:37.633
You really need to keep your eyes on where you're going.

26
00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.133
Right. I'll be more careful.

27
00:01:43.233 --> 00:01:45.600
Oh look-ee what I found!

28
00:01:45.666 --> 00:01:46.966
What? What? Tell us!

29
00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:49.566
Or perhaps we'd better take it to Officer Jenny!

30
00:01:49.633 --> 00:01:51.300
Yeah, like that's gonna happen.

31
00:01:51.366 --> 00:01:53.900
So, taking a peek is what's going to happen instead.

32
00:01:53.966 --> 00:01:55.666
Wobbuffet.

33
00:01:55.733 --> 00:01:59.166
Maybe it's a step-by-step map of the road to riches!

34
00:01:59.233 --> 00:02:01.400
- Eh?
- Oh, my, so handsome!

35
00:02:01.466 --> 00:02:04.466
Wow! It's a picture of none other than Steven Stone!

36
00:02:04.533 --> 00:02:07.800
- Hm?
- Steven Stone? No way.

37
00:02:07.866 --> 00:02:11.100
Right! He's the strongest trainer in Hoenn!

38
00:02:11.166 --> 00:02:14.533
- He's the champion!
- The champion?

39
00:02:18.366 --> 00:02:19.666
Ta-da!

40
00:02:19.733 --> 00:02:22.400
They're my homemade sweet treats and Poké Puffs!

41
00:02:22.466 --> 00:02:24.666
- After a battle, it's teatime!
- Pika!

42
00:02:24.733 --> 00:02:26.933
Looks delish!

43
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.433
Tree!

44
00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.733
- Yummy! Wow!
- Treecko!

45
00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.433
Heh. Thank you! Eat all you want!

46
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.033
- Hey, look at them go!
- Denne-ne!

47
00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.900
Yum. There's nothing like a great dessert.

48
00:02:41.966 --> 00:02:44.600
All I have to do is eat enough of this...

49
00:02:44.666 --> 00:02:48.666
Mm! And in no time, I'll become a powerful trainer just like Ash.

50
00:02:48.733 --> 00:02:50.300
- Huh.
- Pika.

51
00:02:50.366 --> 00:02:52.333
Yeah. You were amazing.

52
00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.166
It didn't matter what kind of situation came up,

53
00:02:55.233 --> 00:02:58.366
it had to be victory and nothing else!

54
00:02:58.433 --> 00:03:00.466
Now I know what to do to win a Gym Badge!

55
00:03:00.533 --> 00:03:02.966
I learned so much from watching you!

56
00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:05.633
And I wrote it all down so I wouldn't forget a thing!

57
00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.433
- Wow, thanks a lot.
- Pika.

58
00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:11.466
Actually, it's the Pokémon who totally deserve to get all the credit.

59
00:03:11.533 --> 00:03:14.700
That means a badge is proof that everyone worked really hard!

60
00:03:14.766 --> 00:03:17.700
You know, you're so right. I'll make a note of it!

61
00:03:17.766 --> 00:03:19.933
- You don't need a note for that...
- Huh?

62
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.433
-Huh?

63
00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.666
- What's wrong, Sawyer?
- Treecko?

64
00:03:23.733 --> 00:03:25.233
- It's gone.
- Huh?

65
00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.900
- Uh, what's gone?
- What did you lose?

66
00:03:27.966 --> 00:03:30.933
My battle notebook is gone!

67
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.733
I wrote down everything I've seen on my journey.

68
00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.666
- Huh?
- And it's in that notebook!

69
00:03:37.933 --> 00:03:41.033
Maybe I lost it... when I fell.

70
00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:45.733
And here he is. The Champion, Steven Stone!

71
00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:48.233
Working with his partner, Metagross,

72
00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:52.466
Steven's the strongest of all trainers in the Hoenn region!

73
00:03:52.533 --> 00:03:53.866
And as if that's not enough,

74
00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:58.466
he's also heir to the Devon Corporation, Hoenn's largest company!

75
00:03:58.533 --> 00:04:01.566
I like the sound of that.

76
00:04:01.633 --> 00:04:05.033
A quiet little wedding and I'll be all set!

77
00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:08.466
So that means Champion Butterfingers dropped this by mistake.

78
00:04:08.533 --> 00:04:11.600
But where? Where, where, where, where, where, where?

79
00:04:11.666 --> 00:04:14.966
- Where is that charming Champion?
- Finding this was a stroke of luck.

80
00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:17.133
We can learn every one of the Champion's secrets

81
00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.566
to raising the strongest Pokémon ever!

82
00:04:19.633 --> 00:04:22.866
No! Being an heir is the most important thing.

83
00:04:22.933 --> 00:04:27.366
Oh! If I can find the Champion, I can marry into mounds of money!

84
00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:30.366
- Don't be a fool!
- We don't need a stinkin' marriage! Dig?

85
00:04:30.433 --> 00:04:33.233
Look. We'll learn the Champion's secret training techniques

86
00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.433
and control the whole world of Pokémon!

87
00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.000
Yeah, and I hear that gig pays really well!

88
00:04:38.066 --> 00:04:40.600
Wobbuffet.

89
00:04:40.666 --> 00:04:44.766
Come on! So weird! I'm sure I dropped it here.

90
00:04:44.833 --> 00:04:48.100
- I don't see it anywhere.
- I'm sure we'll find it.

91
00:04:48.166 --> 00:04:50.366
- Don't you think, Clemont?
- You're right!

92
00:04:50.433 --> 00:04:52.266
I feel awful about this.

93
00:04:52.333 --> 00:04:54.700
- Pika, pika.
- Treecko, Treecko.

94
00:04:54.766 --> 00:04:57.100
Heh. Thanks a lot, Treecko and Pikachu.

95
00:04:57.166 --> 00:05:00.366
Hey, I know! Why don't we split up and look for it?

96
00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:04.133
Yeah. Good idea. Then we can meet up later at the Pokémon Centre.

97
00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.033
Hm.

98
00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.533
Everyone? Help out!

99
00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.133
- Braixen, brai.
- Pancham.

100
00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.900
Right. You too!

101
00:05:12.966 --> 00:05:14.700
- Luxray.
- Chespin.

102
00:05:14.766 --> 00:05:15.766
By!

103
00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.366
- Any luck?
- Nothing.

104
00:05:38.433 --> 00:05:41.566
- Yeah, same here.
- Not even a teensy trace.

105
00:05:41.633 --> 00:05:44.100
- Denne-ne.
- Any luck, Sawyer?

106
00:05:44.166 --> 00:05:48.366
It's no use. I have to face facts.

107
00:05:48.433 --> 00:05:51.333
- My notebook's really gone.
- Treecko.

108
00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:55.466
Sawyer? You've had that notebook ever since you became a trainer, right?

109
00:05:55.533 --> 00:05:57.466
Is everything you've ever learned in there?

110
00:05:57.533 --> 00:05:58.766
Uh-huh.

111
00:05:58.833 --> 00:06:01.433
All the important stuff that's happened since Hoenn.

112
00:06:02.966 --> 00:06:06.866
Everything that Treecko and I have experienced together.

113
00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.500
- Taillow! Taillow!
- Treecko!

114
00:06:08.566 --> 00:06:11.933
I've been able to look back at my notes before all of my battles.

115
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.466
It's helped me a lot!

116
00:06:16.866 --> 00:06:18.500
I've been through some tough battles,

117
00:06:18.566 --> 00:06:21.233
but I always wrote whatever happened in my notebook.

118
00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.233
I've got notes of every experience!

119
00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:29.933
There's even a photo in there. And it's signed.

120
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.466
It's a picture of Steven Stone, the Hoenn Champion.

121
00:06:33.533 --> 00:06:37.066
- Really? The Champion?
- You actually met Steven Stone?

122
00:06:37.133 --> 00:06:38.266
Yeah!

123
00:06:38.333 --> 00:06:42.600
I'll tell you. I respect trainers and Pokémon who give it their all.

124
00:06:42.666 --> 00:06:45.666
And that includes you. You've got a bright future!

125
00:06:45.733 --> 00:06:50.066
You see, Steven's been spending a lot of his time doing research on Mega Stones,

126
00:06:50.133 --> 00:06:53.700
and he even told me that Treecko's capable of Mega Evolution!

127
00:06:53.766 --> 00:06:55.966
-Once it becomes a Sceptile, of course.

128
00:06:56.033 --> 00:06:58.533
- Treecko.
- So Sceptile can Mega Evolve!

129
00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:01.300
- Pika. Pika.
- It's a dream for Treecko and me.

130
00:07:01.366 --> 00:07:03.933
- Mega Evolution!
- Treecko!

131
00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:08.033
All the amazing stuff I learned from Steven Stone

132
00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.600
was in that notebook as well.

133
00:07:09.666 --> 00:07:13.066
Well, if it's that important, then we have to find it!

134
00:07:13.133 --> 00:07:17.333
Clemont, that's your cue to jump into action with a notebook-searching machine!

135
00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:19.500
But there's not even a trail to follow.

136
00:07:19.566 --> 00:07:21.733
Maybe if we could get the notebook's scent...

137
00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:24.500
Of course! I should've thought of that.

138
00:07:24.566 --> 00:07:27.366
Hey, Slurpuff, come on out and give us a hand!

139
00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:30.166
Slurpuff.

140
00:07:30.966 --> 00:07:32.666
- Wow, you've got a Slurpuff!
- Pika, pi.

141
00:07:32.733 --> 00:07:35.900
- Pi! Pika, pika.
- Slurp!

142
00:07:35.966 --> 00:07:38.566
Licking faces is Slurpuff's way of saying hello.

143
00:07:38.633 --> 00:07:40.633
Denne-ne-ne-ne! Denne-ne!

144
00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:42.600
Awesome! Me too!

145
00:07:42.666 --> 00:07:43.866
Will you please...

146
00:07:43.933 --> 00:07:45.400
That's so cute!

147
00:07:45.466 --> 00:07:47.633
Using Slurpuff is a terrific idea.

148
00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.033
Yeah, Slurpuff can pick up the scent of my notebook

149
00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:51.700
by getting a whiff of my scent.

150
00:07:51.766 --> 00:07:53.366
Slurpuff's got a sense of smell

151
00:07:53.433 --> 00:07:56.633
that's a hundred million times more sensitive than a person's!

152
00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:57.733
- Pika, pika.
- Denne-ne-ne.

153
00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:00.600
- Treecko, Treecko, Treecko!
- Slurpuff!

154
00:08:00.666 --> 00:08:03.533
- Mm! Slurp!
- Pika!

155
00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:05.533
Go for it, and good luck!

156
00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:08.666
Ah! Incredible information!

157
00:08:08.733 --> 00:08:10.766
Oh, be still, my beating heart.

158
00:08:10.833 --> 00:08:13.800
You're so lucky, your heart should be dancin' a jig!

159
00:08:13.866 --> 00:08:17.166
- Wobbuffet!
- Egads, look!

160
00:08:17.233 --> 00:08:19.466
- Sceptile can Mega Evolve too!
- Great!

161
00:08:19.533 --> 00:08:22.533
- I'm listening.
- The Champion's notebook is good readin'.

162
00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.166
Slurp, slurp.

163
00:08:25.333 --> 00:08:27.400
Slurpuff!

164
00:08:27.466 --> 00:08:29.666
Who's this blob?

165
00:08:31.566 --> 00:08:34.733
- Come back!
- That's our book, crook!

166
00:08:34.799 --> 00:08:36.033
Slurp!

167
00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:38.033
- Slurpuff!
- Slurp, slurp. Slurp.

168
00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:41.400
- Slurp, slurp.
- You found it, Slurpuff! Thanks so much!

169
00:08:41.466 --> 00:08:44.266
- Treecko!
- I'm so relieved!

170
00:08:44.333 --> 00:08:46.566
- Where did you find it?
- Slurp, slurp.

171
00:08:46.633 --> 00:08:48.500
Twerps?

172
00:08:50.566 --> 00:08:51.900
- It's Team Rocket!
- Pika!

173
00:08:51.966 --> 00:08:54.166
You give me back my key to the good life!

174
00:08:54.233 --> 00:08:56.900
So you were the ones who stole Sawyer's notebook!

175
00:08:56.966 --> 00:08:59.166
- Hey, do you know them?
- 'Fraid so...

176
00:08:59.233 --> 00:09:01.800
They're bad guys who steal other people's Pokémon.

177
00:09:03.033 --> 00:09:06.533
Hurry up! Give it back. The Champion's notebook is ours!

178
00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:07.866
- Champion?
- Huh?

179
00:09:07.933 --> 00:09:10.800
It isn't his! This notebook belongs to me!

180
00:09:10.866 --> 00:09:16.033
Don't act so twerpish. It's signed by the Champion himself!

181
00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:20.033
And you can be sure the two of us will live happily ever after!

182
00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:23.266
This is an autographed photo I got from Steven Stone.

183
00:09:23.333 --> 00:09:26.033
- You got that dude's autograph?
- No joke?

184
00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:28.000
Honestly?

185
00:09:29.866 --> 00:09:32.533
No! The good life left!

186
00:09:34.066 --> 00:09:36.400
All of that wisdom, down the drain!

187
00:09:36.466 --> 00:09:39.200
Next time, don't drop something so confusing!

188
00:09:39.266 --> 00:09:41.633
Keep your book. We'll take your Pokémon!

189
00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:43.866
That's for all our pain and suffering!

190
00:09:43.933 --> 00:09:49.333
- Pumpkaboo, ten-hut!
- 'Kay, Inkay! It's twerp time!

191
00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:51.666
- Inkay.
- Pumpkaboo.

192
00:09:51.733 --> 00:09:54.000
- Hey, Sawyer, let's go!
- Right!

193
00:09:54.066 --> 00:09:56.000
- Pikachu!
- Treecko!

194
00:09:56.066 --> 00:09:58.600
Who's that Pokémon?

195
00:10:03.066 --> 00:10:05.633
It's Grovyle!

196
00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.866
Grovyle!

197
00:10:11.066 --> 00:10:12.800
Pumpkaboo, Shadow Ball!

198
00:10:12.866 --> 00:10:14.833
Ka-ka-ka-ka-ka-ka-kaboo!

199
00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:16.666
Inkay, time for Psybeam!

200
00:10:16.733 --> 00:10:19.400
Inkay!

201
00:10:19.466 --> 00:10:23.333
All right, Pikachu, Thunderbolt! -Pikachu!

202
00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:24.900
Treecko, Bullet Seed!

203
00:10:25.033 --> 00:10:27.066
Treecko!

204
00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:31.000
Pikachu, Thunderbolt once more!

205
00:10:31.066 --> 00:10:33.300
Pi, Pikachu!

206
00:10:36.033 --> 00:10:39.833
You know, I had a feeling that notebook was a bit gnarly the whole time.

207
00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:41.866
Aw, no good life!

208
00:10:41.933 --> 00:10:45.300
That notebook would have looked great on my coffee table.

209
00:10:45.366 --> 00:10:48.133
- We're blasting off again!
- Wobbuffet!

210
00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:50.633
- Pumpkaboo!
- Inkay!

211
00:10:51.666 --> 00:10:54.833
- Bye! You should be used to that!
- Denne-ne!

212
00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:59.366
- Nice going, Sawyer.
- Thanks! To all of you.

213
00:10:59.433 --> 00:11:01.933
Because of your help, my notebook is safe.

214
00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.600
Treecko!

215
00:11:07.466 --> 00:11:09.633
Bonsoir!

216
00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:13.333
Welcome, my Kalos friends who love their Pokémon so dearly!

217
00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:17.700
Here are the details for the next Pokémon Showcase Rookie Class!

218
00:11:17.766 --> 00:11:19.566
- Here it comes.
- Brai!

219
00:11:19.633 --> 00:11:23.100
- Pancham!
- The site is Dendemille Town.

220
00:11:23.166 --> 00:11:27.566
The home of lush, beautiful mountains and quaint windmills.

221
00:11:27.633 --> 00:11:31.666
- Truly a Pokémon farming paradise!
- It's charming!

222
00:11:31.733 --> 00:11:34.833
All performers watching this, mark your calendars.

223
00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:38.566
Choose your favourite Pokémon and make your entry as quick as you can!

224
00:11:38.633 --> 00:11:41.433
The nearest Pokémon Centre is the place to go.

225
00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:43.666
Key, key, Klefki!

226
00:11:43.733 --> 00:11:49.333
Huh. So Dendemille Town. Wow. That's close to Anistar City!

227
00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.533
- Braixen, Braixen.
- Cham!

228
00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:54.266
- All right. Let's register right away!
- Cham, cham!

229
00:11:55.666 --> 00:11:57.100
- Good luck!
- Huh?

230
00:11:57.166 --> 00:11:59.600
It's time for your second Showcase!

231
00:11:59.666 --> 00:12:03.366
- You'll win this time for sure!
- Braixen!

232
00:12:03.433 --> 00:12:05.166
- Pancham!
- Yes I will!

233
00:12:05.233 --> 00:12:07.666
- So, Ash, where's your next Gym Battle?
- Huh?

234
00:12:07.733 --> 00:12:11.600
Well, you see... I haven't really decided yet.

235
00:12:11.666 --> 00:12:14.266
- How about here? Ta-da!
- Pika?

236
00:12:14.333 --> 00:12:15.933
Anistar City!

237
00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.933
- Uh, Anistar City?
- Pika!

238
00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:22.733
It's a great place to visit. It has this amazing sundial!

239
00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:26.733
And besides, Dendemille Town is right on the way there, heh.

240
00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:29.300
Ah, that's it. Anistar City.

241
00:12:29.366 --> 00:12:32.466
- I'll get my seventh badge there!
- Pika, Pikachu.

242
00:12:32.533 --> 00:12:34.766
Hey, Sawyer, what are you gonna do?

243
00:12:34.833 --> 00:12:38.266
- I'm gonna head for the Coumarine Gym.
- That Gym's awesome!

244
00:12:38.333 --> 00:12:40.266
Coumarine City's amazing, as well!

245
00:12:40.333 --> 00:12:42.266
They've even got a monorail!

246
00:12:42.333 --> 00:12:45.100
If I remember, the Gym Leader is Ramos.

247
00:12:45.166 --> 00:12:49.033
Yeah, and he's strong. Have fun and good luck!

248
00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:51.733
Thanks! I'll work hard.

249
00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:54.433
But before that, I've got a little favour to ask you.

250
00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:55.733
- Hm?
- Pika?

251
00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:01.300
The last time we battled, we had to stop in the middle.

252
00:13:01.366 --> 00:13:04.033
How'd you like to finish it up before we head out?

253
00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:07.433
- So, what are the rules?
- How about we each use three Pokémon?

254
00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:09.533
You heard him, Pikachu. Let's go!

255
00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:11.466
Pika! Pika, pika!

256
00:13:11.533 --> 00:13:14.966
My first Pokémon will be Bagon!

257
00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:17.700
Bagon!

258
00:13:17.766 --> 00:13:19.833
I'll be the referee, if you don't mind.

259
00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:22.700
- Good luck, both of you
- Have a great battle!

260
00:13:22.766 --> 00:13:27.000
Ash versus Sawyer. Battle begin!

261
00:13:28.866 --> 00:13:32.100
- Use Quick Attack! Go!
- Pi, pi, pi!

262
00:13:32.166 --> 00:13:35.633
- Use Headbutt!
- Bagon!

263
00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:37.066
Wow. Pikachu's fast!

264
00:13:37.133 --> 00:13:39.333
Gon!

265
00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:41.333
Now, counter with Dragon Breath!

266
00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:42.933
Bagon!

267
00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:46.300
- Use Thunderbolt!
- Pikachu!

268
00:13:48.133 --> 00:13:50.433
- All right, use Iron Tail!
- Pika...

269
00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:53.833
- Chu!
- Ba!

270
00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:56.733
Iron Tail from up there? Now, Dragon Claw, go!

271
00:13:56.800 --> 00:13:58.700
Bagon!

272
00:14:08.166 --> 00:14:09.166
Pika.

273
00:14:09.233 --> 00:14:12.633
Bagon is unable to battle. Pikachu's the winner!

274
00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:16.700
- Wow. That was so fast!
- And Pikachu looked really strong.

275
00:14:16.766 --> 00:14:20.700
Bagon, thanks a lot. Now, you take a good rest.

276
00:14:20.766 --> 00:14:25.066
Ah. Your Pikachu sure is tough, Ash.

277
00:14:25.133 --> 00:14:27.133
- Pikachu.
- Don't worry!

278
00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:30.066
Your Bagon's gonna keep on getting stronger, you'll see!

279
00:14:30.133 --> 00:14:33.166
Right! Now, Slurpuff, you're next!

280
00:14:36.033 --> 00:14:37.066
Slurpuff!

281
00:14:37.133 --> 00:14:39.900
OK I'm going with Hawlucha!

282
00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:43.400
Cha!

283
00:14:43.466 --> 00:14:46.766
Electro Ball's perfect for Flying types. Go!

284
00:14:48.466 --> 00:14:51.466
- Dodge it and use Karate Chop!
- Ha!

285
00:14:51.533 --> 00:14:53.966
- What?
- Lu, ha-cha!

286
00:14:54.033 --> 00:14:56.766
Slur, Slurpuff!

287
00:14:56.833 --> 00:15:00.266
No, Slurpuff! OK, what's my next move?

288
00:15:00.333 --> 00:15:02.566
Flying Press!

289
00:15:02.633 --> 00:15:05.866
Ha-cha!

290
00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:10.566
- Slurpuff...
- Ha!

291
00:15:11.833 --> 00:15:15.533
Slurpuff is unable to battle. Hawlucha's the winner!

292
00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:19.033
Way to go, Hawlucha! Return!

293
00:15:21.033 --> 00:15:24.300
I'm sorry. See, I couldn't do a thing.

294
00:15:24.366 --> 00:15:25.766
- Sawyer?
- Huh?

295
00:15:25.833 --> 00:15:27.400
When your Pokémon gets hit,

296
00:15:27.466 --> 00:15:29.700
a trainer's gotta stay cool, no matter what!

297
00:15:29.766 --> 00:15:31.200
Uh, right!

298
00:15:31.266 --> 00:15:34.933
See, if a trainer hesitates, then the Pokémon will hesitate too.

299
00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:38.166
After all, Pokémon and trainer are battling together as one!

300
00:15:38.233 --> 00:15:39.633
'Kay, I understand.

301
00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:41.300
During his Gym Battle,

302
00:15:41.366 --> 00:15:43.400
that's just what Ash and his Pokémon were doing.

303
00:15:43.466 --> 00:15:46.533
I'll have to put everything I've ever jotted down into this battle!

304
00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:50.033
Ready to go, Sawyer? Now, Frogadier, I choose you!

305
00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:52.900
Frogadier.

306
00:15:52.966 --> 00:15:55.633
My third Pokémon's Treecko!

307
00:15:57.233 --> 00:16:00.066
Tree! Treecko!

308
00:16:00.133 --> 00:16:02.933
Don't forget I've got the advantage with this type match-up.

309
00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:05.366
We'll just see about that.

310
00:16:05.433 --> 00:16:08.933
- Frogadier, Aerial Ace!
- Frogadier!

311
00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:10.833
That's a Flying-type move!

312
00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:12.366
Froga!

313
00:16:12.433 --> 00:16:14.400
-That was super effective!

314
00:16:14.466 --> 00:16:17.366
- Treecko, are you OK?
- Treecko.

315
00:16:17.433 --> 00:16:20.733
- All right, Bullet Seed!
- Treecko!

316
00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:23.733
- That's really effective, too!
- Keep it going, Treecko!

317
00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:25.333
Fast as you can!

318
00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:29.766
Fro... ga... dier!

319
00:16:29.833 --> 00:16:31.066
Frogadier!

320
00:16:31.133 --> 00:16:33.833
But why? I can't panic, no matter what!

321
00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:35.233
Agility, let's go!

322
00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:40.566
- Now, Water Pulse!
- Frogadier!

323
00:16:40.633 --> 00:16:42.066
Treecko!

324
00:16:42.133 --> 00:16:46.066
- Tree... tree...
- Treecko! Can you still go on?

325
00:16:46.133 --> 00:16:48.366
Ko!

326
00:16:48.433 --> 00:16:52.233
Treecko!

327
00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:53.300
Huh?

328
00:16:53.366 --> 00:16:54.966
Treecko!

329
00:16:55.033 --> 00:16:56.500
- What's that?
- Could it be?

330
00:17:06.933 --> 00:17:10.866
Grovyle! Grov! Grov!

331
00:17:10.933 --> 00:17:13.500
It evolved!

332
00:17:13.566 --> 00:17:15.466
- Ah.
- I'll take a look.

333
00:17:15.533 --> 00:17:19.966
Grovyle. The Wood Gecko Pokémon, and an evolved form of Treecko.

334
00:17:20.033 --> 00:17:25.966
Grovyle has powerful legs, which allow it to move quickly and jump with great power.

335
00:17:26.033 --> 00:17:29.366
That just happened because Grovyle could sense your passion!

336
00:17:29.433 --> 00:17:31.700
My passion, huh?

337
00:17:31.766 --> 00:17:36.133
Grovyle, you ready? Let's win this!

338
00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:38.933
Grovyle! Grov. Grovyle!

339
00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:40.366
Grov, grov, Grovyle!

340
00:17:40.433 --> 00:17:43.366
Wow. Awesome. You know Leaf Blade!

341
00:17:43.433 --> 00:17:45.433
Now. Double Team!

342
00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:46.533
Frog, frog, frog.

343
00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:48.800
- Grovyle! Leaf Blade!
- Grovyle!

344
00:17:48.866 --> 00:17:50.066
Grovyle!

345
00:17:50.133 --> 00:17:53.033
Froga! Frog!

346
00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:54.933
- Froga!
- Grovyle!

347
00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:57.233
- Frogadier!
- Grovyle!

348
00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:58.866
- Grov?
- Frogadier!

349
00:17:58.933 --> 00:18:01.366
- Use Aerial Ace!
- Grovyle?

350
00:18:03.566 --> 00:18:05.200
Grovyle!

351
00:18:05.266 --> 00:18:06.933
'Kay, use Leaf Blade!

352
00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:08.000
- Gadier!
- Grov!

353
00:18:08.066 --> 00:18:10.000
- Frog, frog, froga!
- Grov, grov, grov.

354
00:18:10.066 --> 00:18:13.333
- Now, use Cut!
- Frogadier!

355
00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:15.800
Grovyle!

356
00:18:15.866 --> 00:18:18.333
- This has turned into a great battle!
- Yeah!

357
00:18:18.400 --> 00:18:22.433
Grovyle and I are battling together as one!

358
00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:26.066
- Use Aerial Ace!
- Frogadier! Frogadier!

359
00:18:26.133 --> 00:18:27.566
- Jump! Go!
- Grov!

360
00:18:29.133 --> 00:18:30.566
Ga?

361
00:18:30.633 --> 00:18:32.166
- Now what?
- Grovyle can jump!

362
00:18:32.233 --> 00:18:34.400
- So high!
- Grovyle, Bullet Seed!

363
00:18:34.466 --> 00:18:36.566
Grovyle!

364
00:18:36.633 --> 00:18:40.833
- Uh! Use Water Pulse!
- Frogadier!

365
00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:46.300
Now, Grovyle, use Leaf Blade!

366
00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:50.133
Grovyle!

367
00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:53.266
- Huh?
- Grovyle.

368
00:18:53.333 --> 00:18:55.866
- Water Pulse, come on!
- Frogadier!

369
00:18:55.933 --> 00:18:57.366
Grovyle!

370
00:18:58.500 --> 00:18:59.600
Frog.

371
00:18:59.666 --> 00:19:01.900
-Denne.

372
00:19:03.066 --> 00:19:04.400
Gr... Grovyle?

373
00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:10.400
- Grovyle.
- Uh!

374
00:19:10.466 --> 00:19:13.533
Grovyle.

375
00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:15.433
No, Grovyle!

376
00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.766
Grovyle is unable to battle.

377
00:19:17.833 --> 00:19:19.433
Frogadier's the winner!

378
00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:23.700
That was great, Frogadier. You battled really well.

379
00:19:23.766 --> 00:19:25.900
- Awesome job!
- Pikachu.

380
00:19:25.966 --> 00:19:27.433
Frog.

381
00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:30.200
- Hey, Grovyle, are you OK?
- Grovyle!

382
00:19:30.266 --> 00:19:32.433
- Grovyle.
- Huh?

383
00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:34.366
Froga.

384
00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:36.366
Grovyle.

385
00:19:36.433 --> 00:19:39.366
Whoa. Both of you are really pumped up!

386
00:19:39.433 --> 00:19:41.866
I think they'll be good rivals!

387
00:19:41.933 --> 00:19:45.366
- Let's keep getting stronger, Grovyle!
- Grovyle!

388
00:19:45.433 --> 00:19:48.200
Sawyer, good luck with your Gym Battles!

389
00:19:48.266 --> 00:19:49.400
Thanks.

390
00:19:49.466 --> 00:19:51.866
I'll be cheering for you in your Pokémon Showcase!

391
00:19:51.933 --> 00:19:53.266
Thanks so much.

392
00:19:53.333 --> 00:19:56.433
And this time, I'll get that Princess Key for sure!

393
00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:59.600
Hey, Ash? Thanks so much for everything you've done.

394
00:20:00.733 --> 00:20:03.600
For battling me and for all the stuff you've taught me.

395
00:20:03.666 --> 00:20:06.966
- No problem. Good luck at the gym!
- Pika.

396
00:20:07.033 --> 00:20:09.900
Thanks a lot, Ash. Same to you at the Anistar Gym.

397
00:20:09.966 --> 00:20:12.800
- Win your seventh badge!
- Right.

398
00:20:15.933 --> 00:20:19.200
Now that our heroes have gotten to know Sawyer,

399
00:20:19.266 --> 00:20:22.733
the young man from Hoenn, they prepare to set off on their journey,

400
00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:25.666
while Sawyer prepares to set off on his.

401
00:20:25.733 --> 00:20:29.500
And so, until Ash and Sawyer meet again...

402
00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:36.700
Well, Ash, next time we battle, things will be different.

403
00:20:36.766 --> 00:20:41.000
I'm going to get stronger and stronger, and then I'll be the winner!

404
00:20:42.166 --> 00:20:44.866
..the journey continues!
